    {
      "id": "claim_85d4f8419f5545b89d9af484ecc75563",
      "statement": "The token package's Payload embeds standard RFC7519 jose claims plus step/JWK (sha, sans), OIDC (at_hash, azp, email...), Azure, K8sSA service-account, and nested GCP/AWS cloud claims, on a JSONWebToken wrapper around go.step.sm/crypto/jose.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://token/parse.go#L29-L62",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:a968cb37b30cea89a7af2413a6b86314d92a6a18e087d155702d72c24309f49f:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_d5ce293df49342afaeb824467ff0c805",
      "statement": "Payload.Type() classifies tokens by structural priority: nested google/amazon/azure claims, then Kubernetes service-account issuer, then presence of sha/sans (JWK), then a complete OIDC claim set, else Unknown; X5C and Nebula are header-defined types in the same enum.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://token/parse.go#L65-L82",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:cbaf83d7f80c558c1a01da83a546424f778247b1a120986647a5739c5851f438:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_b35bd177023e4e04b2c802c29fa03ec0",
      "statement": "token.Parse verifies the JWT signature with a supplied key, while token.ParseInsecure uses UnsafeClaimsWithoutVerification and must only be used for inspection, not authorization.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://token/parse.go#L139-L166",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:ebedd4e4a891c3791f37dd10d799eccb896ceb2fbf5938b25662ddfe16808bcf:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
